      "hints": [
        "For the AP, express $b$ in terms of $a$ using common differences: $\\frac{3}{2}a - a = b - \\frac{3}{2}a$.",
        "For the GP, set $18^2 = a(b + 3)$.",
        "Substitute $b = 2a$ to form a quadratic in $a$ and solve."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the arithmetic progression property for terms $a, \\frac{3}{2}a, b$:\n$$\\frac{3}{2}a - a = b - \\frac{3}{2}a \\implies \\frac{1}{2}a = b - \\frac{3}{2}a \\implies b = 2a$$",
        "Use the geometric progression property for terms $a, 18, b + 3$:\n$$18^2 = a(b + 3) \\implies 324 = a(b + 3)$$",
        "Substitute $b = 2a$ into the geometric equation:\n$$324 = a(2a + 3) \\implies 2a^2 + 3a - 324 = 0$$",
        "Factorise the quadratic and solve for positive $a$ and $b$:\n$$(a - 12)(2a + 27) = 0 \\implies a = 12 \\quad (\\text{since } a > 0)$$\n$$b = 2(12) = 24$$\n$$a = 12, \\quad b = 24$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
